  "term": "narcotherapy",
  "definition": "Narcotherapy is the use of intravenous barbiturate drugs such as sodium amytal or sodium pentothal to produce a relaxed, more talkative state. Related therapeutic uses of this drug-assisted state include narcosuggestion, narcosynthesis, and narcoanalysis.",
